(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Frame is a frame of a thread's stack (HES8 (a))."] [19 15 "// a case's slots; an apply frame's arguments"] [22 11 "// the thread's arena's top when the frame was pushed (arena.go)"] [30 8 "// restores the masking state n on return"] [35 8 "// keepAlive#'s value kept reachable while its action runs"] [38 1 "// Thread is a Haskell thread: its stack, its resumption, its masking state (0 unmasked, 1 masked"] [39 1 "// uninterruptibly, 2 masked interruptibly: getMaskingState#'s numbers)."] [50 23 "// what it waits on: *MVar, *Thunk, *sleep, stmWait, nil when runnable"] [51 23 "// the throwTo#s waiting for it to accept them (rts.go)"] [52 23 "// the TVars its transaction read (a retry's wake-up, the collector's reachability)"] [59 2 "// locked to its capability (forkOn#), and that capability's number (forkOn#'s, modulo enabled_capabilities)"] [62 2 "// bound to an OS thread (the threaded way: the main thread, forkOS's, an in-call's; threaded.go)"] [64 2 "// an interruptible block (MVar, delay, STM retry): an asynchronous exception may be delivered"] [66 2 "// the allocation counter (bytes, counting down), whether its limit is enabled, allocWords when last accounted"] [72 1 "// Machine is hsi's machine: the loader, the address space, the threads."] [82 2 "// the threads waiting on descriptors (fdwait.go) and the last poll of them"] [90 2 "// the weak pointers not yet dead, and the collector's memos of what code keeps alive (rts.go)"] [109 49 "// compiled functions called directly since the last bounce (aot.go)"] [110 49 "// a pure primop's arguments"] [111 49 "// a thread's frames at most (SetStackLimit): StackOverflow past it"] [112 49 "// a tail call's arguments"] [116 55 "// a program's own C (cprog.go), or nil"] [117 55 "// objects' identities as C sees them (cprog.go)"] [118 2 "// the RTS's C API (rtsapi.go): the HaskellObj words, stable_ptr_table and its size, the capability's address"] [122 21 "// C finalizers running (runCFins): a callback from one is GHC\\'s error"] [123 21 "// +RTS -xq: the allocation limit's grace, bytes (0: GHC's 100k)"] [124 2 "// the threaded way (threaded.go, HES84 (a)): the program linked -threaded; enabled_capabilities, +RTS -N's count and"] [125 2 "// the label's address; the safe foreign calls in flight and their returns; the spark pool"] [141 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [144 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [151 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [192 2 "// in place (HES73): the popped slot's fields written, no frame copied (its x and n are zero: pop clears them)"] [198 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [201 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [210 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [228 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update; a transaction aborts first and reruns from its start"] [229 3 "// after the wake-up (review 189, F2, the user's decision: the other threads never see its writes)"] [247 4 "// two update frames in a row (the lower thunk's evaluation is entering this one): squeezed as GHC's"] [248 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [249 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [250 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [256 5 "// in place, as pushCase"] [266 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [275 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [279 30 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [290 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [330 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [340 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [343 2 "// the two frequent frames read in place (HES73): no frame copied out, its pointers cleared"] [377 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value lost as GHC's"] [390 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [393 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [400 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [401 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [406 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [407 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [434 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [449 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [450 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [451 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [459 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [462 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [472 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [482 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [483 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [490 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [491 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [499 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [539 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [544 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [550 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [579 3 "// the program's own C faulted (cprog.go): the process a signal's end, as a C program's"] [602 1 "// reason writes why hsi stopped (HES43 (b)), a word beside its message, on a line of its own: \"hsi-reason: WORD\" (bin/hsi"] [603 1 "// check records it as the result's :reason, a class matches it by its :reasons)."] [606 1 "// fatalReason is the reason of a stop of hsi's own by its message: what it lacks (a primop, a Cmm primcall, a C function,"] [607 1 "// a function pointer, the RTS's API) or a state it cannot go on from (a deadlock), else fatal."] [626 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [653 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [667 6 "// a safe foreign call returning or the first delay expiring, whichever comes first"] [675 6 "// asleep in poll(2) until a descriptor is ready or the first delay expires (awaitEvent)"] [691 5 "// every thread waits for a safe foreign call (the threaded way): until one returns"] [739 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [740 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [741 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [753 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [768 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [773 5 "// the allocation limit, checked every 256 bounces (GHC: at each nursery block, 4 KiB)"] [778 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [792 3 "// a case continuation run by ret may be compiled code that ran a yield# or a direct call to the budget's end"] [793 3 "// (HES74 (c): -O1's inline yield#, a forked thread's first chance): the slice ends here too, as it would"] [794 3 "// after the interpreter's eval of the alternative"] [805 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [810 3 "// exitScheduler (threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in foreign calls left"] [822 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [836 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [845 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [854 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [859 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [860 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [861 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [864 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [865 1 "// holds what a few of GHC's words do, so a -K limit is reached at a comparable depth, not the same one)."] [868 1 "// SetStackLimit sets a thread's stack limit to bytes (+RTS -K)."] [877 1 "// unwindThunk is a thunk under evaluation an exception unwinds: reverted to unevaluated (asynchronous), or made to raise"] [878 1 "// again (synchronous); its waiters woken."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[203 24] [215 27] [246 18] [255 19] [282 23] [345 26] [378 36] [438 37] [492 35] [558 20] [635 27] [635 44] [746 17] [774 44] [888 24]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


